course: dictionary
lesson: 3684
title: Flamenco: a word from Spain
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name things from other countries and cultures. Flamenco is one of them. You can work out its meaning from the words around it, so read the context first. «Flamenco comes from Andalusia in southern Spain, with Romani roots, and uses guitar, singing, clapping and fast, strong footwork.» The place names and the instruments tell you it is a style of music and dance.
explain: Look for clues about feelings too. The same sentence says flamenco «can show proud, angry or sad feelings, not only happy ones.» So flamenco is not always cheerful. The words not only tell you that the author is adding a surprising detail, so you should notice it.
explain: Flamenco can also be an adjective, a word that describes things linked to this style. A flamenco dress is a dress in this style, and a flamenco guitar is a guitar played in it. Ask yourself whether the word names a thing or describes one. The word after it often gives you the answer.
fact: Flamenco is a lively, passionate kind of music, singing and dance from southern Spain.
fact: Flamenco comes from Andalusia, a region in southern Spain.
fact: Flamenco uses guitar playing, hand clapping and fast stamping feet.
fact: The Roma (Gitano) people of Spain helped create flamenco.
fact: Flamenco can show many feelings, including proud, angry, sad and happy.
exercise: «Flamenco comes from Andalusia in southern Spain.» Where does flamenco come from? | The island of Ireland | Central Italy | Northern France | *Southern Spain
exercise: A girl wears a flamenco dress with frills and polka dots. What is a flamenco dress? | A dress for swimming in the sea | *A dress linked to the flamenco style, with frills and polka dots | A plain grey dress for school | A dress made of glass
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that names a musical instrument: «Flamenco uses guitar, singing, clapping and fast, strong footwork.» | clapping | footwork | *guitar | singing
test: Flamenco can show proud, angry or sad feelings. Which of these is a feeling it can show? | Silly | Asleep | *Sad | Hungry
test: Who helped create flamenco? | Scottish shepherds | *The Roma people of Spain | Ancient Egyptians | Vikings
exam: Which of these best describes flamenco? | A sport played on ice | *A lively style of music, singing and dance from southern Spain | A type of frilly hat worn by sailors | A quiet bedtime song from Scotland
